  "raw_html": "<button type='button' role='link' class='btn btn-link p-0 text-start' id='link_1' aria-label=\" Union of India Through its Secretary & Ors. versus SGT Girish Kumar and Ors. Etc. pdf\"  class='noToken' href='#' onclick=javascript:open_pdf('1','2026','2026_2_615_626','2026INSC149'); ><font size='4'> <strong>UNION OF INDIA THROUGH ITS SECRETARY & ORS.<span class='fst-italic'> versus </span>SGT GIRISH KUMAR AND ORS. ETC. </strong>- <span class='escrText'>[2026] 2 S.C.R. 615</span><span class='ncDisplay'>2026 INSC 149</span><input type='hidden' id='cnr' value=ESCR010000582026></button></font><br><strong>Coram : PAMIDIGHANTAM SRI NARASIMHA<sup style=\"color: #268e97;font-size: 22px;top: 0;\" class=\"tooltip-sup\" data-tooltip=\"Author\">*</sup></strong><br> Issue for Consideration Issue arose for consideration whether the benefit of arrears of disability pension can be restricted to three years prior to filing of the original applications before the tribunal. Headnotes&dagger; Armed Forces Tribunal Act, 2007 &ndash; Claim for arrears of disability pension &ndash; Benefit of arrears of disability pension, if can be restricted to three years prior to filing of the original applications before the tribunal: Held: Disability pension is grounded not merely in length of service, but in the impairment<br><strong class='caseDetailsTD' ><span style='color:#212F3D' > Decision Date :</span><font color='green'> 12-02-2026</font><span style='color:#212F3D' > | Case No :</span><font color='green'> CIVIL APPEAL No. 6820/2018</font>  <span style='color:#212F3D' > | Direction Issue :</span><font color='green'> Appeals by the Union of India dismissed. Appeals by the ex-servicemen allowed.</font> <span style='color:#212F3D' > |  Bench :</span><font color='green'> 2 Judges</font></strong><div class='row my-1 mt-2 border bg-light'><div class='col-auto'><a href='#' class='btn btn-outline-secondary btn-sm my-1' onclick=open_splitview('1','2026','2026_2_615_626','2026INSC149','S')